From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wlanapi: WlanGetProfileList, WlanConnect, WlanDisconnect, WlanDeleteProfile, WlanReasonCodeToString

Spec stubs before (Discord's and OBS's binaries name them; Wi-Fi tools use them), now through sg-netctl (NetworkManager) like the scan of 7853. A profile is a saved Wi-Fi network (wifi saved), named after its SSID as Windows names the profiles it makes, an all-user profile. WlanConnect checks its arguments, the interface and the profile, then connects on a thread of its own and tells the notification callback (connection_start; connection_attempt_fail with a reason -- a refused key is WLAN_REASON_CODE_MSMSEC_PSK_MISMATCH_SUSPECTED, a network out of range NETWORK_NOT_AVAILABLE; connection_complete), as Windows does: a saved profile with its saved key, a temporary profile (XML: SSID as hex or name, open / WPA-PSK / WPA2-PSK / WPA3-SAE, the key material on sg-netctl's standard input, never a command line), an open network by SSID (discovery_unsecure); 802.1X, WEP, a protected key, discovery_secure and ad hoc are ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED. NetworkManager keeps a temporary profile's connection (not set to connect automatically); Windows forgets it. WlanDisconnect disconnects the adapter (disconnecting, disconnected), WlanDeleteProfile forgets the network (ERROR_NOT_FOUND for no such profile), WlanReasonCodeToString describes the reason codes. wlanapi.h: the profile, connection and notification types, reason codes.
